1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thttp://www.steinheim-institut.de/cgi-bin/epidat?id=ffb-3388
2 CONT
2 CONT ombstone Inscription: Leah Gutllen, wife of the Aharon Bonn to the cheerful man | Justice dwelted | 3 | in her. Here is carved the grave | a dignified and respected woman | Ms. Leah Gutlen, | 6 | Daughter of Mr. Moshe, his memory 
2 CONC for blessing, buried | (on) Day 4, 23 of the first Adar 369 of the small count. Your soul is part of the bundle of life, Amen
2 CONT
2 CONT Steinheim Institute Commentary:
2 CONT
2 CONT Dating Died, Friday, February 27 , 1609 Zln 2-3a: Isa 1,21. Zl 3b: cf. Isa 22:16. Rhyme up - wa in lines 2-4. Abbreviation no longer recognizable; Sentence separator: '' shaped
2 CONT
2 CONT Tombstone Description: Stele with a recessed lettering field, double chamfered frame and arched finish. The writing field is closed with a three-pass, above it a header in smaller letters on the frame, following the course of the 
2 CONC curve, in it Zln 2-3. House sign no condition Only two fragments of the upper end and one fragment of the middle writing field have survived from this tombstone, the rest is missing. Some of the inscription had to be added after H
2 CONC o. The fragments come from Hill A.
2 CONT
2 CONT About the person Lea Gutlen married around 1563 and lived in the house as a cheerful man.
2 CONT
2 CONT About the family Father: Mosche Bonn zum Kessel, son of Jaakow (No. ffb-0653 , not with Ho, ET around 1568, died November 20, 1549?) Mother: Sprintz Husband: Aharon from Türkheim, called Bonn, son of Natan (No. ffb-0057 , Ho 5563,
2 CONC  ET around 1623) Children: Natan Bonn to the traffic lights (No. ffb-0629 , Ho 171, ET 25.XI.1629); Mosche Bonn to the Bisemknopf (No. ffb-0220 , Ho 730, ET 29.VII.1647); Schlom Bonn to the cheerful man, then to the golden swan (n
2 CONC ot with Ho, ET 16.V.1662); Heart Bonn to the happy man (not with Ho, ET 24.X.1682); Sore, wife of Feibesch Bacharach to Bisemknopf, then wife of Gumpel KaZ to the white steed, then wife of Herz KaZ to the green door (No. ffb-0449 
2 CONC , Ho 804, ET 10.XII.1655)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources / secondary literature ET 27.II.1609 Dietz, p. 38f. (Gatte, Vater ???) Lö, Jewish gravestones, in: Blätter ..., II. Jg., No. 8, p. 60 Ho, Rabbinen, p. 43, 277 (Gatte) Ho 420 HoNam. P. 700: Gutle Bonn z. happy. Man Ho Ed: Z
2 CONC l 1 וריליכמן, in the text וריליכה מאן. The rest of the inscription had to be largely supplemented after Ho. His line layout is incorrect. HoSt 1774
