1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Act #798: 16.03.1683, folio 62: transfer of Natan CAHEIN to his son Alexandre CAHEIN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Act #949: 18.04.1685, p 39: receipt; Ennée ZEY, wife of Alexandre CAHENNE Jew of Metz, declares to have received from sieur Jean DIOCHE, admodiator of the land and seigniory of Apremont, the sum of 100 white ecus at 8 francs and 2
2 CONC  large Messins one; signature in Hebrew: "Hinlen bat Issachar Zeye".
2 CONT
2 CONT Metz Memorbuch #604 [English Translation]: The right rabbi Alexandre, son of rabbi Nathan Cahen, who donated to the poor of here, Metz, and to those of the Holy Land.  Died and buried on Sunday, the eve of the new moon of Iyyar 54
2 CONC 63 [15 Apr 1703].
2 CONT
2 CONT "Senderlen Cohen" p.286 et 288 Faustini
