1 OCCU riche banquier, syndic des Juifs de Metz
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Salomon Moïse, rich banker, died on 03.10.1717 according to the inventory after death (indication of Mr. Philippe Blachais); the date indicated by the Memorbuch (notice n° 805: "the rich and illustrious syndic and 
2 CONC shtadlan the haver Salomon Moïse son of the haver Alexander Cahen") is 21.10.1718
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorbuch #805 [English Translation]: The rich and illustrious trustee and shtadlan, Haver Solomon Moses, son of Haver Alexandre Cahen, who was for some years the leader of our community in Metz, and devoted himself to the individ
2 CONC uals and the community. He made various interventions, went several times far away for the affairs of the community and knew how to defend its cause... He was accepted by the great ones. He was humble and led the community with ge
2 CONC ntleness... He was hospitable, especially to the wise. He ordered before his death that 9,000 livres be taken from his inheritance to be used as a capital, the income of which would be distributed by his heirs to the wise men to s
2 CONC tudy with the sons of the poor. His heirs also gave 300 livres to the charity of our community, 300 for the poor of the Holy Land as he had requested, not to mention other gifts to the sages and the poor, made while he lay sick in
2 CONC  bed, and the charities that were distributed between his death and the burial and during the days of mourning to the holy brotherhoods to study for the salvation of his soul. His other benefits are mentioned in his will. He died 
2 CONC on Friday evening and was buried on Sunday 28 Tishrei 4579 [23 October 1718]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Shlomo Zalman Cohen", "Zalman Cahen", "Salomon Moïse fils du haver Alexandre Cahen"... p. 285 et 286 Faustini
2 CONT
2 CONT date de naissance : 1660?1670 ?
