1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Born in 1794 to Josef and Jeanette Müller, Moses was raised in the town of Wissembourg until the age of 15. In 1809, the family moved to Danzig, where Moses studied under Rabbi Marcus Noah Perls, the Chief Rabbi of
2 CONC  Danzig.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT By the time this family lived Altona was a city of its own and the cemetery Bornkampsweg also belonged to Altona. Altona was also Danish once and in 1938 the city became part of Hamburg.Altona has one of the oldest Jewish Cemeteri
2 CONC es in Europe.
