2 CONT " Rabbi Suskind Stern dealt in jewellery and was a moneychanger, and was listed as one of the most highly taxed individuals in the Jewish community.  His sons, Isaac Suskind and Samuel Stern, took over the family business on his d
2 CONC eath and continued to run it as partners. They also provided commissary services to the emperor's troops, supplying flour etc. "
